Explanation: These two systemd-named packages are the image's sysusers and tmpfiles providers (config/packages.yaml); APT reads pins in stanza order, so this exemption must precede the wildcard below to keep them installable.
Package: systemd-standalone-sysusers systemd-standalone-tmpfiles
Pin: version *
Pin-Priority: 500

Explanation: Spaced Linux uses sysvinit; rolling upgrades must retain it.
Package: systemd systemd-*
Pin: version *
Pin-Priority: -1
